w a  big uh  blockage at the ports and then you'd  have problems with supply and supply  chain obviously going into uh you know  the christmas period which uh you know  would be damaging for everybody  when we say damaging uh are we talking  about an annoyance or are we talking  about something  much bigger than that  i think we're talking about something  much bigger than that i mean we've seen  already the practicalities of brexit in  terms of moving good uh you know uh  back and forth um and uh this has become  something of an issue now of course  we've had the the the covert situation  which has had muddied the waters to a  certain extent but i think no doubt  already some of the challenges that are  being had are brexit related  and  you know i think you would see certainly  a major step up of that it doesn't take  very much at the ports  by way of a slow down a couple of  minutes can lead to  significant uh delays and  tailbacks on the roads so it could be  major  how likely do you think that there is  going to be  a serious problem and let's measure it  this way  that um  people are even now beginning to buy  their christmas presents for their  children they're thinking about  what they're going to  give  each other at christmas what uh  decorations all the rest of it  do you think that we are going to see  christmas interrupted in any serious way  because of this  looming dispute  it's it trevor is difficult to say i  mean we're obviously in a highly  political situation and and all sides  will be weighing that up  and you know i think that  the consequences of this are potentially  major to go into the end of year period  with that consequence you know i i know  that that will be something at front of  mind for politicians on both sides um  but i'm afraid it's not not to be ruled  out and unfortunately you know the  people who are going to end up paying  the price for this  are you know normal people like us and  the businesses that get caught in the  cross